-4s"></i><i style="left:28%;--d:10s;--x:0px;animation-delay:-5s"></i><i style="left:57%;--d:11s;--x:20px;animation-delay:-6s"></i><i style="left:86%;--d:12s;--x:40px;animation-delay:-7s"></i><i style="left:15%;--d:13s;--x:-40px;animation-delay:-8s"></i></div><div class="wl-w wl-hero-g"><div class="wl-hero-t"><p class="wl-hand">pull on a pair&hellip;</p><h1>Socks that hug back.</h1><p class="wl-lead">Woolies is a cosy guide to wool socks: why wool keeps feet warm and dry, which thickness to wear for every day and adventure, and how to wash, mend and even knit your own.</p><div class="wl-hero-a"><a class="wl-btn" href="#warm">Find my warmth</a><a class="wl-btn wl-btn-o" href="#knit">Knit a pair</a></div></div>
<div class="wl-hero-v"><figure class="wl-mit"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1704034809858-28521d052ea7?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=600&q=75" alt="a pair of socks lying on a table" width="520" height="600" fetchpriority="high"></figure><figure class="wl-mit wl-mit-s"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1689191007449-badd99afa7e3?auto=format&fit=crop&w=300&h=300&q=75" alt="feet in white socks beside a cup of coffee" width="300" height="300" fetchpriority="high"></figure><div class="wl-hang"><svg viewBox="0 0 160 220" class="wl-sk wl-sk-1" aria-hidden="true"><defs><clipPath id="hs1"><path d="M40 6h70v120q0 14 10 24l18 18q14 16 0 32t-32 2L46 160Q36 150 38 130z"/></clipPath></defs><g clip-path="url(#hs1)"><rect width="160" height="220" class="b"/><rect y="6" width="160" height="22" class="cuff"/><g class="st"><rect y="44" width="160" height="10"/><rect y="64" width="160" height="10"/></g><path d="M100 150l60 0v80h-80z" class="heel"/><circle cx="125" cy="190" r="26" class="toe"/></g><path d="M40 6h70v120q0 14 10 24l18 18q14 16 0 32t-32 2L46 160Q36 150 38 130z" class="ol"/></svg><svg viewBox="0 0 160 220" class="wl-sk wl-sk-3" aria-hidden="true"><defs><clipPath id="hs2"><path d="M40 6h70v120q0 14 10 24l18 18q14 16 0 32t-32 2L46 160Q36 150 38 130z"/></clipPath></defs><g clip-path="url(#hs2)"><rect width="160" height="220" class="b"/><rect y="6" width="160" height="22" class="cuff"/><g class="st"><rect y="44" width="160" height="10"/><rect y="64" width="160" height="10"/></g><path d="M100 150l60 0v80h-80z" class="heel"/><circle cx="125" cy="190" r="26" class="toe"/></g><path d="M40 6h70v120q0 14 10 24l18 18q14 16 0 32t-32 2L46 160Q36 150 38 130z" class="ol"/></svg></div><p class="wl-note">100% toasty</p></div></div></section>

<section class="wl-s wl-jy"><div class="wl-w"><div class="wl-sh wl-sh-c"><p class="wl-hand">from sheep to sock</p><h2 class="rv">A short, woolly journey</h2></div><ol class="wl-jy-l stg"><li class="rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1484557985045-edf25e08da73?auto=format&fit=crop&w=360&h=360&q=75" alt="a white sheep standing on green grass" width="360" height="360" loading="lazy"></figure><span>1</span><b>Fleece</b><p>Sheep are shorn once a year in spring.</p></li><li class="rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1598871956222-26b66d6559fe?auto=format&fit=crop&w=360&h=360&q=75" alt="brown and white rolls of yarn" width="360" height="360" loading="lazy"></figure><span>2</span><b>Yarn</b><p>The wool is washed, combed and spun.</p></li><li class="rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1773747203071-4a34106c39a4?auto=format&fit=crop&w=360&h=360&q=75" alt="hands knitting with blue and grey yarn" width="360" height="360" loading="lazy"></figure><span>3</span><b>Stitch</b><p>Yarn is knitted into tubes, heels and toes.</p></li></ol></div></section>

<section class="wl-s wl-wm" id="warm"><div class="wl-w wl-wm-g"><div><p class="wl-hand">tool one</p><h2 class="rv">Sock warmth picker</h2><p class="wl-p">Tell us what you&rsquo;re doing and how cold it is. We suggest a cushion, a wool blend and a height, and show the sock to match.</p>
<p class="wl-lb">What are you doing?</p><div class="wl-chips" id="wm-a" role="group" aria-label="Activity"><button type="button" data-v="0">Lounging at home</button><button type="button" data-v="1">Everyday shoes</button><button type="button" data-v="2" class="on">Hiking</button><button type="button" data-v="3">Skiing</button><button type="button" data-v="4">Work boots</button></div>
<label class="wl-lb" for="wm-t">Outside temperature: <b id="wm-tv">35&deg;F</b></label><input type="range" id="wm-t" min="-10" max="75" step="5" value="35" class="wl-rng"><div class="wl-therm" aria-hidden="true"><i id="wm-tb"></i></div>
<figure class="wl-wm-i rv rv-c"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1612216553330-af1656ea1c15?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=220&q=75" alt="brown leather boots standing in the snow" width="560" height="220" loading="lazy"></figure></div>
<div class="wl-tag" aria-live="polite"><div class="wl-tag-v"><svg viewBox="0 0 160 220" class="wl-sk wl-sk-p" aria-hidden="true"><defs><clipPath id="ps"><path d="M40 6h70v120q0 14 10 24l18 18q14 16 0 32t-32 2L46 160Q36 150 38 130z"/></clipPath></defs><g clip-path="url(#ps)"><rect width="160" height="220" class="b"/><rect y="6" width="160" height="22" class="cuff"/><g class="st"><rect y="44" width="160" height="10"/><rect y="64" width="160" height="10"/></g><path d="M100 150l60 0v80h-80z" class="heel"/><circle cx="125" cy="190" r="26" class="toe"/></g><path d="M40 6h70v120q0 14 10 24l18 18q14 16 0 32t-32 2L46 160Q36 150 38 130z" class="ol"/></svg></div><p class="wl-hand">our pick</p><h3 id="wm-r">Medium cushion crew</h3><dl><div><dt>Cushion</dt><dd id="wm-c"></dd></div><div><dt>Wool blend</dt><dd id="wm-w"></dd></div><div><dt>Height</dt><dd id="wm-h"></dd></div></dl><p id="wm-n" class="wl-tag-n"></p></div></div></section>

<section class="wl-s wl-kn" id="knit"><div class="wl-w wl-kn-g"><div class="wl-kn-card" aria-live="polite"><p class="wl-hand">your pattern notes</p><ul class="wl-kn-r"><li><span>Cast on</span><b id="kn-co">64</b><small>stitches</small></li><li><span>Leg length</span><b id="kn-lg">7</b><small>inches</small></li><li><span>Foot before toe</span><b id="kn-ft">7.8</b><small>inches</small></li><li><span>Yarn needed</span><b id="kn-y">90</b><small>grams</small></li></ul><p class="wl-small" id="kn-n"></p></div>
<div><p class="wl-hand">tool two</p><h2 class="rv">Sock knitting calculator</h2><p class="wl-p">Measure around the ball of your foot and from heel to toe, then add your knitting gauge. We work out how many stitches to cast on for a snug fit.</p>
<label class="wl-lb" for="kn-c">Foot circumference: <b id="kn-cv">9 in</b></label><input type="range" id="kn-c" min="6" max="12" step=".25" value="9" class="wl-rng">
<label class="wl-lb" for="kn-l">Foot length: <b id="kn-lv">9.5 in</b></label><input type="range" id="kn-l" min="6" max="12" step=".25" value="9.5" class="wl-rng">
<label class="wl-lb" for="kn-g">Gauge (stitches per inch): <b id="kn-gv">8</b></label><input type="range" id="kn-g" min="6" max="10" step=".5" value="8" class="wl-rng"><figure class="wl-kn-i rv rv-c"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1731399211410-e3ffe1560310?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=220&q=75" alt="a stack of three knitted blankets" width="560" height="220" loading="lazy"></figure></div></div></section>

<section class="wl-cab"><figure class="wl-cab-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1741948924635-13a7ddbc6a05?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&h=700&q=75" alt="a cosy cabin glowing in the snowy woods at night" width="1600" height="700" loading="lazy"></figure><div class="wl-w wl-cab-t rv"><p class="wl-hand">the coziest fact</p><p class="wl-cab-q">Wool can hold about a third of its weight in moisture and still feel dry, which is why wool socks stay warm even after a long walk in the snow.</p></div></section>

<section class="wl-gd"><div class="wl-w"><h2 class="rv">Curl up with a guide</h2><div class="wl-gd-g"><a class="wl-gc rv" href="why-wool-socks-guide.html"><svg viewBox="0 0 160 220" class="wl-sk wl-sk-2" aria-hidden="true"><defs><clipPath id="gs1"><path d="M40 6h70v120q0 14 10 24l18 18q14 16 0 32t-32 2L46 160Q36 150 38 130z"/></clipPath></defs><g clip-path="url(#gs1)"><rect width="160" height="220" class="b"/><rect y="6" width="160" height="22" class="cuff"/><g class="st"><rect y="44" width="160" height="10"/><rect y="64" width="160" height="10"/></g><path d="M100 150l60 0v80h-80z" class="heel"/><circle cx="125" cy="190" r="26" class="toe"/></g><path d="M40 6h70v120q0 14 10 24l18 18q14 16 0 32t-32 2L46 160Q36 150 38 130z" class="ol"/></svg><div><p class="wl-hand">guide one</p><b>Why Wool Socks?</b><p>Warmth, dryness, smell and the difference between merino and the rest.</p></div></a><a class="wl-gc wl-gc-b rv" href="wash-and-darn-wool-socks-guide.html"><svg viewBox="0 0 160 220" class="wl-sk wl-sk-4" aria-hidden="true"><defs><clipPath id="gs2"><path d="M40 6h70v120q0 14 10 24l18 18q14 16 0 32t-32 2L46 160Q36 150 38 130z"/></clipPath></defs><g clip-path="url(#gs2)"><rect width="160" height="220" class="b"/><rect y="6" width="160" height="22" class="cuff"/><g class="st"><rect y="44" width="160" height="10"/><rect y="64" width="160" height="10"/></g><path d="M100 150l60 0v80h-80z" class="heel"/><circle cx="125" cy="190" r="26" class="toe"/></g><path d="M40 6h70v120q0 14 10 24l18 18q14 16 0 32t-32 2L46 160Q36 150 38 130z" class="ol"/></svg><div><p class="wl-hand">guide two</p><b>Wash &amp; Darn Wool Socks</b><p>Gentle washing, drying, and mending holes so they last for years.</p></div></a></div></div></section>

